Each patch applies to a copy of rtl/ (patch -p1). run_mutations.py runs the directed
tests and seeds 0-99 against every one and expects a failure.

m01 arbiter pointer never advances              should hit A3
m02 extra grant when two channels request       should hit A1
m03 grant to a channel that isn't requesting    should hit A2
m04 fifo full flag one entry late               should hit A4
m05 issue fsm pops an empty fifo                should hit A5
m06 cmd_addr moves while waiting on cmd_ready   should hit A6
m07 wlast one beat early                        scoreboard
m08 source address never increments             scoreboard
m09 tail burst rounded up to a full burst       scoreboard
m10 read data routed to channel id + 1          scoreboard
